_.WDb=[{title:"re:cap",Vj:"re:cap uses Gemini Managed Agents to power the customer-facing advisory experience behind Capital Advisory and most of its operational agents.",slug:"recap",Ok:"https://aistudio.google.com/agents",thumbnail:{url:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/recap/recap_thumbnail.jpg",alt:"re:cap showcase preview"},Rj:[{label:"re:cap",url:"https://www.re-cap.com"}],mi:[{label:"Gemini 3.7 Flash",url:"/docs/models/gemini-3.7-flash"}],modules:[{type:"hero",content:{date:"October 19, 2026",
headline:"How re:cap is building Capital Advisory with Gemini Managed Agents",Ku:"On real customer questions, Gemini Managed Agents answered 2.6\u00d7 faster at 73% lower model cost, with answers grounded in live data. Now the team is using Managed Agents to power the customer-facing advisory experience behind its new product and most of its operational agents.",authors:[{name:"Arne Zeising",role:"CTO, re:cap"}],thumbnail:{src:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/recap/recap_thumbnail.jpg",
type:"image",alt:"re:cap showcase hero"}}},{type:"stats",content:{stats:[{value:"2.6\u00d7",description:"Faster average responses than the previous implementation"},{value:"5\u00d7",description:"Faster slowest answers than the previous implementation"},{value:"73%",description:"Lower model costs than the previous implementation"}]}},{type:"cta",content:{link:"https://aistudio.google.com/agents"}},{type:"text",content:{body:'\n            <p>\n              <a href="https://www.re-cap.com/">re:cap</a> is a Berlin-based fintech that arranges debt financing and provides a capital strategy and advisory platform to startups and SMEs across Europe. Its newest product, Capital Advisory, is designed to help founders and finance teams understand what financing they could realistically raise based on their business and financial data.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              At the center of the experience is a Gemini Managed Agent. It is one of several agents re:cap runs in production on Gemini Managed Agents.\n            </p>'}},
{type:"text",content:{body:"\n            <p>\n              Founders start with a Capital Readiness Assessment: re:cap researches their company, asks a few questions and calculates where they stand. Once they sign in, they can ask detailed follow-up questions about their results, financing options, and company financials.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Those conversations are handled by Gemini Managed Agents, with access to re:cap's data through MCP and a set of skills the team developed specifically for Capital Advisory.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              For re:cap, this wasn't just a new architecture. The engineering team had already built the experience on another agent platform, giving them an opportunity to test two different implementations on the same workload.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Testing Gemini Managed Agents on real customer questions</h2>"},body:'\n            <p>\n              re:cap took 29 common customer questions from Capital Advisory that had run on their previous setup and replayed them using Gemini Managed Agents, in the same order.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Gemini Managed Agents delivered fast, lower-cost answers grounded in live platform data.\n            </p>\n            <table>\n              <thead>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope="col">re:cap Capital Advisory Benchmark</th>\n                  <th scope="col">Gemini Managed Agents (Gemini 3.7 Flash)</th>\n                  <th scope="col">Previous managed agent implementation</th>\n                </tr>\n              </thead>\n              <tbody>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope="row">Mean answer time</th>\n                  <td>25.4 sec</td>\n                  <td>65.6 sec</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope="row">Slowest answer</th>\n                  <td>46 sec</td>\n                  <td>236 sec</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope="row">Mean cost per question</th>\n                  <td>6.0\u00a2 (\u221273%)</td>\n                  <td>22.4\u00a2</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope="row">Answer style</th>\n                  <td>Concise (preferred by the team)</td>\n                  <td>More detailed</td>\n                </tr>\n              </tbody>\n            </table>\n            <p>\n              That works out to approximately <b>2.6\u00d7 faster average responses, 5\u00d7 faster slowest answers and 73% lower model costs</b> in the re:cap Capital Advisory Benchmark. Every answer stayed tied to live platform data across all 29 questions.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              These results are specific to re:cap\'s workload and implementation, rather than a general benchmark of the two platforms. Costs are at list prices. Advisory is where answer quality matters most, and Gemini Managed Agents delivered it faster and at lower cost.\n            </p>'}},
{type:"quote",content:{quote:"Agents are becoming how we run re:cap, both for our customers and for our own team. Gemini Managed Agents gave us the speed and cost to do that at high volume, and it works the way we already build: skills as files, shipped like the rest of our code.",author:"\u2014 Arne Zeising, CTO of re:cap"}},{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Building a capital advisor that can work with customer data</h2>"},body:"\n            <p>\n              Capital Advisory is designed to answer a fairly difficult question: given what re:cap knows based on the financial data of a company, what financing could that company realistically raise?\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              re:cap didn't turn the entire product into a Managed Agent. The founder's journey has three stages, and each gives the model only as much freedom as the job needs, with a matching guardrail:\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              <b>Research: an agent loop.</b> A founder enters their company website. Through ADK, Gemini chooses its next step from a fixed set of tools, such as Google Search, reading web pages, running code and re:cap's own research tools. It runs for every visitor, so it has to be thorough and fast.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              <b>Assessment: a fixed pipeline.</b> The founder answers a few guided questions. re:cap's own code calculates every number; Gemini only reads the answers and writes the summary, both in a fixed format. Speed and cost come first.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              <b>Advisory: an open conversation.</b> After the assessment, founders ask questions re:cap can't predict: why an option fits, what the alternatives are, or anything else in their account. This is the part built on Gemini Managed Agents. Answer quality comes first.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"images",content:{items:[{image:{src:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/recap/recap-capital-advisory-journey.svg",alt:"Diagram of the three stages of Capital Advisory: Research uses the Gemini API and ADK with a fixed set of tools, Assessment uses the Gemini API with typed outputs, and Advisory uses Gemini Managed Agents scoped to one customer account."}}]}},{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>One platform for customers and operations</h2>"},body:"\n            <p>\n              In Capital Advisory, Gemini Managed Agents powers:\n            </p>\n            <ul>\n              <li><b>Deep dives on live financials:</b> revenue, liquidity and profitability analyses on the company's own bank and accounting data.</li>\n              <li><b>Work on the founder's own spreadsheets:</b> analyse an uploaded workbook or export re:cap data into it.</li>\n              <li><b>Data readiness in the conversation:</b> which inputs are missing or out of date, and how to fix them.</li>\n            </ul>\n            <p>\n              Behind it, several operational agents run on the same platform, built the same way, each with its own skills and permissions. They classify inbound companies for the sales team, check the quality of a company's financial data, and draft company updates and support replies for a person to approve. Because all of these agents draw on one shared set of skills, an improvement made once reaches every agent that uses it.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>How the Managed Agent works</h2>"},body:"\n            <p>\n              When a founder starts asking questions, re:cap starts a Gemini Managed Agents environment for their account. The agent can access re:cap's customer data through MCP, along with the skills re:cap has built for capital-advisory tasks. It is the same re:cap MCP server customers can already connect to their own AI agents, so Capital Advisory needed no separate data layer and reaches only the data the founder's own account can see.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              The founder doesn't leave re:cap or interact with a separate Gemini product.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"images",content:{items:[{image:{src:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/recap/recap-capital-advisory-architecture.svg",alt:"Architecture diagram: the founder chats in re:cap, which exchanges messages with Gemini Managed Agents. Each founder gets their own agent environment, built from an agent definition (model, skills and connectors) that CI syncs from GitHub, and it reads live company data through the same re:cap MCP server that founders can connect to their own AI agents."}}]}},
{type:"text",content:{body:"\n            <p>\n              The setup also works well with the way re:cap already develops agents internally. The team maintains its skills in a plugin-style directory structure, with instructions and shared knowledge stored as files. Gemini Managed Agents lets re:cap bring that structure into the agent's environment, rather than rebuilding every skill as a separate platform object.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Three choices let re:cap put Capital Advisory in front of customers the day after the benchmark, and they work for any team running agents in production:\n            </p>\n            <ul>\n              <li><b>One definition per agent.</b> A single file names the agent's instructions, skills, tools and model, versioned like code.</li>\n              <li><b>Skills ship like code.</b> They live on GitHub, and CI updates every agent when one changes.</li>\n              <li><b>One environment per customer account.</b> The agent only ever sees that customer's data.</li>\n            </ul>"}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Where Capital Advisory goes from here</h2>"},body:"\n            <p>\n              The rollout is complete: every customer using Capital Advisory is now served by Gemini Managed Agents.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              The broader goal is to help founders understand financing options beyond the debt financing re:cap arranges. If debt isn't the right instrument, Capital Advisory helps the founder understand what else may fit.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"quote",content:{quote:"Every founder should know what financing they can raise before they ask for it. Capital Advisory gives them that answer from their own data, whatever the right option turns out to be.",author:"\u2014 Arne Zeising, CTO of re:cap"}},{type:"text",content:{body:'\n            <p>\n              Read the <a href="/docs/agents">Managed Agents documentation</a> to start building with Gemini Managed Agents.\n            </p>'}},{type:"related_cases",content:{Bk:["instalily",
